# icCommunity API

Telegram-style **channels** on ICPay. Creators post text; members read (queries).
Public channels appear in `/channels`; private channels join via invite code only.

---

## Types

| Type | Values |
|------|--------|
| `CommunityVisibility` | `#open` (listed) · `#inviteOnly` (private invite link) |
| `CommunityAccess` | `#free` · `#paid` (0.1–10 ICP one-time join) |

Paid join transfers ICP from member → creator custodial balance (memo `icCommunity:<slug>`).

---

## Endpoints

| Method | Kind | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `createCommunityChannel` | update | Name, slug, bio, visibility, access, priceE8s, optional inviteSecret |
| `joinCommunityChannel` | update | Free or paid join; private needs `inviteCode` |
| `leaveCommunityChannel` | update | Member leaves (owner cannot) |
| `postCommunityMessage` | update | Creator only |
| `pinCommunityMessage` | update | Creator pins one message |
| `deleteCommunityMessage` | update | Creator soft-deletes |
| `getCommunityChannel` | query | Public metadata |
| `listPublicCommunityChannels` | query | Paginated public directory |
| `listMyCommunityChannels` | query | Channels caller joined or owns |
| `listCommunityMessages` | query | After `afterId`, capped `limit` |
| `isCommunityMember` | query | Membership check |

---

## Read access (messages)

- Owner or member: always
- Public + free: anyone (discovery without join)
- Private or paid: members only

---

## Limits (`Config.mo` + `IcCommunityStorage.mo`)

| Limit | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Channels per owner | 5 |
| Paid price | 0.1 – 10 ICP |
| Name | 80 chars |
| Bio | 280 chars |
| Slug | 3–32, `a-z0-9_` |
| Message | 2000 chars |
| Messages per channel | 2000 (oldest dropped) |
| List page | 50 max |

Rate limits: create 3/min, join 10/min, post 20/min per caller.

---

## Files

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `types.mo` | `Community*` types |
| `storage/IcCommunityStorage.mo` | Maps + constants |
| `repositories/IcCommunityRepository.mo` | CRUD |
| `validators/IcCommunityValidator.mo` | Input checks |
| `services/IcCommunityService.mo` | Business logic |
| `api/v1/IcCommunity.mo` | Candid mixin |
| `main.mo` | Stable maps + wire |
| `testing/services/IcCommunityService.test.mo` | Unit tests |

---

## NOT in v1

- Channel delete, edit bio, regenerate invite
- Replies, reactions, media in messages
- Monthly subscription renewals
- Platform fee split on paid join (100% to creator)

---

## Cycle burn (estimates)

Source: ICPay `cycles-and-cost` skill (measured on this canister) + icCommunity
storage shape. **Measure on mainnet** before quoting runway to users:

```bash
B0=$(dfx canister status icp_wallet_backend --network ic | grep Balance | tr -dc '0-9')
for i in $(seq 10); do dfx canister call icp_wallet_backend postCommunityMessage '(...)' --network ic; done
B1=...
echo $(( (B0-B1)/10 ))
```

### What costs cycles

| Action | Call type | Typical burn | Notes |
|--------|-----------|--------------|-------|
| `listCommunityMessages` | **query** | **~0** | Free on IC — use SWR on open, no polling |
| `getCommunityChannel` | query | ~0 | |
| `listPublicCommunityChannels` | query | ~0 | Paginated; not full-registry scan |
| `listMyCommunityChannels` | query | ~0 | Index by principal |
| `createCommunityChannel` | update | **~10–25M** | Few map writes |
| `joinCommunityChannel` (free) | update | **~10–20M** | Member row + count |
| `joinCommunityChannel` (paid) | update + **ledger** | **~50–90M** | Ledger call dominates (~40M+) |
| `postCommunityMessage` | update | **~8M → ~25M** | Grows with message count (array copy) |
| `pin` / `delete` / `leave` | update | **~8–15M** | Single channel touch |

ICPay idle floor today ≈ **1.43B cycles/day** (whole wallet, not icCommunity alone).

### Storage (idle floor)

Rough bytes per channel (stable memory):

| Data | @100 msgs, 100 members | @1000 msgs, 1000 members |
|------|------------------------|--------------------------|
| Channel metadata | ~1 KB | ~1 KB |
| Members (map + index) | ~30–80 KB | ~300–800 KB |
| Messages (text ~200 chars avg) | ~50 KB | ~500 KB |
| **Total per channel** | **~100 KB** | **~1 MB** |

Extra idle from icCommunity storage is small vs wallet baseline until thousands
of channels. Rule: **~4M cycles/GiB/day** → 100 KB ≈ **400 cycles/day**.

### Scenario totals (one-time setup burn)

Assumes mid-range estimates; paid joins include one ICP ledger call.

| Scenario | Updates | Est. cycles | ≈ idle-days* |
|----------|---------|-------------|--------------|
| **1 channel, 0 members, 100 posts** | 1 create + 100 post | **~1.0–1.5B** | ~0.7–1 |
| **1 channel, 100 free joins, 100 posts** | +100 join | **~2.0–3.0B** | ~1.4–2 |
| **1 channel, 100 paid joins, 100 posts** | +100 paid join | **~6–9B** | ~4–6 |
| **10 channels** (same each) | ×10 | **~10×** above | |
| **100 channels, 100 msgs each** | heavy seed | **~100–300B** | weeks of idle |

\* Compared to 1.43B/day wallet idle — not calendar days of runway.

### Daily usage (healthy pattern)

| Pattern | Updates/day | Queries/day | Est. burn/day |
|---------|-------------|-------------|---------------|
| Creator posts 3×/day, 50 members read once (SWR) | 3 post | 50×2 query | **~30–60M** |
| Same + 10 new free joins | +10 join | same | **~130–200M** |
| Same + 10 paid joins | +10 paid | same | **~600M–1B** |

**Reads are free** — the cheap model is: burn on **join** (especially paid) and
**post**, not on feed views.

### Design choices that keep burn low

1. All feed/history/list paths are `shared query`.
2. No polling — fetch when user opens `/channels/@slug`.
3. Cap 2000 msgs/channel (oldest dropped).
4. Page size max 50 (`MAX_LIST`).
5. Paid join = one ledger call (unavoidable); creator revenue should exceed
   canister cost (0.1 ICP join >> ~0.00001 ICP worth of cycles).

### Break-even (paid channel)

At ~70M cycles per paid join and ~1.5T cycles/ICP:

- Cycle cost per paid join ≈ **0.00005 ICP** (order of magnitude)
- Min price 0.1 ICP → canister cost **&lt;0.05%** of revenue per join

Measure after deploy; do not treat this table as billing truth.
